# Prompt para Restaurar Integración Biométrica

Copia y pega el siguiente prompt en una nueva sesión de chat con tu asistente de IA para restaurar todo el trabajo realizado.

---

**Rol:** Eres un desarrollador experto en sistemas Full Stack y IoT.
**Objetivo:** Integrar un sistema de asistencia biométrica (huella dactilar) en el proyecto `hr-hub` existente.
**Contexto:** El proyecto es un sistema de RRHH construido con React, Vite, Supabase y Shadcn/UI. Existe un dispositivo ESP32 con lector de huellas R307 que debe comunicarse con el sistema.

## Fase 1: Análisis del Sistema

Primero, realiza un análisis detallado de la estructura actual del proyecto `hr-hub` para entender dónde encajan los nuevos componentes.
- Revisa [package.json](file:///c:/Users/salif/Downloads/Nuevo%20RRHH/hr-hub/package.json), `supabase/migrations`, y `src/pages`.
- Identifica la tabla `profiles` y cómo se gestionan los usuarios.

## Fase 2: Implementación

Una vez analizado, aplica los siguientes cambios EXACTAMENTE como se describen a continuación.

### 1. Base de Datos (Supabase)

Ejecuta/Crea las siguientes migraciones para añadir `biometric_id`, `biometric_templates` y `device_commands`.

**Archivo:** `supabase/migrations/20251125_biometric_integration.sql`
```sql
-- Add biometric_id to profiles
ALTER TABLE public.profiles 
ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS biometric_id INTEGER UNIQUE CHECK (biometric_id > 0 AND biometric_id <= 127);

-- Create biometric_templates table
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS public.biometric_templates (
  id uuid PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  user_id uuid REFERENCES auth.users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE NOT NULL,
  finger_id INTEGER NOT NULL, -- 1 or 2 (primary or backup finger)
  template_data TEXT NOT NULL, -- Base64 encoded template
  created_at timestamptz DEFAULT now(),
  updated_at timestamptz DEFAULT now(),
  UNIQUE(user_id, finger_id)
);

ALTER TABLE public.biometric_templates ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

CREATE POLICY "Admins can manage biometric templates"
  ON public.biometric_templates FOR ALL TO authenticated
  USING (public.has_role(auth.uid(), 'superadmin') OR public.has_role(auth.uid(), 'admin_rrhh'));

CREATE POLICY "Users can view own biometric templates"
  ON public.biometric_templates FOR SELECT TO authenticated
  USING (auth.uid() = user_id);

-- Create device_commands table
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS public.device_commands (
  id uuid PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
  device_id text NOT NULL, -- e.g., 'ESP32-001'
  command_type text NOT NULL, -- 'ENROLL', 'RESTART', etc.
  payload jsonb, -- e.g., { "biometric_id": 1 }
  status text DEFAULT 'pending' CHECK (status IN ('pending', 'processing', 'completed', 'failed')),
  created_at timestamptz DEFAULT now(),
  updated_at timestamptz DEFAULT now()
);

ALTER TABLE public.device_commands ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

CREATE POLICY "Admins can manage device commands"
  ON public.device_commands FOR ALL TO authenticated
  USING (public.has_role(auth.uid(), 'superadmin') OR public.has_role(auth.uid(), 'admin_rrhh'));

-- Index for faster polling
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_device_commands_device_status ON public.device_commands(device_id, status);
```

### 2. Backend (Supabase Edge Function)

Crea la función `biometric-api` para manejar la comunicación con el ESP32.

**Archivo:** [supabase/functions/biometric-api/index.ts](file:///c:/Users/salif/Downloads/Nuevo%20RRHH/hr-hub/supabase/functions/biometric-api/index.ts)
```typescript
import { serve } from "https://deno.land/std@0.168.0/http/server.ts"
import { createClient } from "https://esm.sh/@supabase/supabase-js@2"

const corsHeaders = {
    'Access-Control-Allow-Origin': '*',
    'Access-Control-Allow-Headers': 'authorization, x-client-info, apikey, content-type',
}

serve(async (req) => {
    if (req.method === 'OPTIONS') {
        return new Response('ok', { headers: corsHeaders })
    }

    try {
        const supabaseClient = createClient(
            Deno.env.get('SUPABASE_URL') ?? '',
            Deno.env.get('SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY') ?? ''
        )

        const url = new URL(req.url)
        const path = url.pathname.split('/').pop()

        if (path === 'check-id') {
            const biometric_id = url.searchParams.get('biometric_id')
            if (!biometric_id) throw new Error('Missing biometric_id')

            const { data, error } = await supabaseClient
                .from('profiles')
                .select('id, full_name')
                .eq('biometric_id', parseInt(biometric_id))
                .single()

            if (error || !data) {
                return new Response(JSON.stringify({ exists: false }), {
                    headers: { ...corsHeaders, 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
                    status: 404
                })
            }

            return new Response(JSON.stringify({ exists: true, name: data.full_name, user_id: data.id }), {
                headers: { ...corsHeaders, 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
                status: 200
            })
        }

        if (path === 'attendance') {
            const { biometric_id, device_id } = await req.json()
            if (!biometric_id) throw new Error('Missing biometric_id')

            // 1. Get user_id from biometric_id
            const { data: user, error: userError } = await supabaseClient
                .from('profiles')
                .select('user_id, full_name')
                .eq('biometric_id', biometric_id)
                .single()

            if (userError || !user) {
                throw new Error('User not found for this biometric ID')
            }

            // 2. Insert attendance record
            const now = new Date()
            const today = now.toISOString().split('T')[0]
            const { data: existing, error: existingError } = await supabaseClient
                .from('attendance_records')
                .select('*')
                .eq('user_id', user.user_id)
                .eq('attendance_date', today)
                .order('created_at', { ascending: false })
                .limit(1)
                .single()

            let result;

            if (existing && !existing.check_out) {
                // Update as check_out
                const { data, error } = await supabaseClient
                    .from('attendance_records')
                    .update({
                        check_out: now.toISOString(),
                        status: 'completado'
                    })
                    .eq('id', existing.id)
                    .select()
                    .single()

                if (error) throw error
                result = { type: 'Salida', timestamp: now, name: user.full_name }
            } else {
                // Insert new check_in
                const { data, error } = await supabaseClient
                    .from('attendance_records')
                    .insert({
                        user_id: user.user_id,
                        attendance_date: today,
                        scheduled_start: '09:00', // Default
                        scheduled_end: '18:00',   // Default
                        check_in: now.toISOString(),
                        status: 'presente',
                        notes: `Biometric: ${device_id}`
                    })
                    .select()
                    .single()

                if (error) throw error
                result = { type: 'Entrada', timestamp: now, name: user.full_name }
            }

            return new Response(JSON.stringify(result), {
                headers: { ...corsHeaders, 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
                status: 200
            })
        }

        if (path === 'enroll') {
            const { biometric_id, template, finger_id } = await req.json()

            // Get user_id
            const { data: user, error: userError } = await supabaseClient
                .from('profiles')
                .select('user_id')
                .eq('biometric_id', biometric_id)
                .single()

            if (userError || !user) throw new Error('User not found')

            const { error } = await supabaseClient
                .from('biometric_templates')
                .upsert({
                    user_id: user.user_id,
                    finger_id: finger_id || 1,
                    template_data: template
                })

            if (error) throw error

            return new Response(JSON.stringify({ success: true }), {
                headers: { ...corsHeaders, 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
                status: 200
            })
        }

        if (path === 'poll-commands') {
            const device_id = url.searchParams.get('device_id')
            if (!device_id) throw new Error('Missing device_id')

            const { data, error } = await supabaseClient
                .from('device_commands')
                .select('*')
                .eq('device_id', device_id)
                .eq('status', 'pending')
                .order('created_at', { ascending: true })
                .limit(1)
                .single()

            if (error && error.code !== 'PGRST116') { // PGRST116 is "No rows found"
                throw error
            }

            if (!data) {
                return new Response(JSON.stringify({ command: null }), {
                    headers: { ...corsHeaders, 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
                    status: 200
                })
            }

            // Mark as processing
            await supabaseClient
                .from('device_commands')
                .update({ status: 'processing' })
                .eq('id', data.id)

            return new Response(JSON.stringify({ command: data }), {
                headers: { ...corsHeaders, 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
                status: 200
            })
        }

        if (path === 'command-status') {
            const { command_id, status, result } = await req.json()

            const { error } = await supabaseClient
                .from('device_commands')
                .update({ status, payload: result ? { result } : undefined }) // Optionally store result
                .eq('id', command_id)

            if (error) throw error

            return new Response(JSON.stringify({ success: true }), {
                headers: { ...corsHeaders, 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
                status: 200
            })
        }

        throw new Error('Invalid path')

    } catch (error) {
        return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: error.message }), {
            headers: { ...corsHeaders, 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
            status: 400
        })
    }
})
```

